    "updated_at": "2021-04-01T14:53:50Z",
    "body": "Oh I see, you're comparing it against the bash implementation? I didn't quite understand what that sentence in \"additional context\" meant at first.\r\n\r\nThe cmd_duration module is shell-dependent because every shell has its own way of recording/reporting time taken in commands. bash doesn't have this at all, so we have to hack together a homegrown version that behaves differently than shells that have this as a built-in feature.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what the correct way to document this is (#2478 is a similar issue, though it also seems to have some other bugs attached to it).",
